|{{flag|Chile}}
|[[Santiago]]
|25–28 January
|President Rousseff traveled to Santiago to attend the first CELAC–EU summit. She cut her trip short to return to Brazil after the [[Kiss nightclub fire]] in [[Santa Maria, Rio Grande do Sul|Santa Maria]].<ref>{{cite news|title=Brazil Fire Highlights Larger Cause for President Rousseff|url=https://www.voanews.com/a/brazil-fire-highlights-larger-cause-for-president-rousseff-reuters/1594070.html|work=[[Voice of America]]|date=28 January 2013|access-date=15 October 2026}}</ref>
|-
|{{flag|South Africa}}
|[[Durban]]
|25–27 March
|{{further|5th BRICS summit}}President Rousseff traveled to Durban to attend the [[5th BRICS summit]].<ref>{{cite news|title=Developing nations to meet at BRIC beach party in South Africa|url=https://www.cnbc.com/2013/03/25/developing-nations-to-meet-at-bric-beach-party-in-south-africa.html|work=[[CNBC]]|date=25 March 2013|access-date=15 October 2026}}</ref>
|-
|{{flag|Russia}}
|[[Saint Petersburg]]
|5–6 September
|President Rousseff traveled to Saint Petersburg to attend the [[2013 G20 Saint Petersburg summit]].<ref>{{cite news|title=Brazilian Leader Postpones State Visit Over Spying Concerns|url=https://www.wwno.org/2013-09-17/brazilian-leader-postpones-state-visit-over-spying-concerns|work=[[WWNO]]|date=17 September 2013|access-date=15 October 2026}}</ref>
|}

On 17 September 2013, President Rousseff cancelled her state visit to Washington, D.C., on 3 October 2013, because of alleged spying by the United States that targeted Brazil.<ref>{{cite news|title=Brazil cancels U.S. visit over spy claims|url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/world/2013/09/17/obama-brazi-dilma-rousseff-national-security-agency/2826211/|work=USA Today|access-date=17 September 2013|first1=David|last1=Jackson|date=17 September 2013}}</ref>

