==2015==
The following international trips were made by President Dilma Rousseff in 2015:
{| class="wikitable"
! Country
! Areas visited
! Date(s)
! Notes
|-
|{{flag|Mexico}}
|Mexico City
|25–27 May
|{{further|Brazil–Mexico relations}}
President Rousseff travelled to Mexico for a [[state visit]]. President Rousseff met with President [[Enrique Peña Nieto]] at the [[National Palace (Mexico)|National Palace]] to discuss agreements on commercial cooperation, [[investment protection]], tourism, and [[Brazil–Mexico relations#Trade relations|trade]].<ref>{{cite news|title=EPN receives President Dilma Rousseff at National Palace|url=https://www.eluniversal.com.mx/articulo/english/2015/05/26/epn-receives-president-dilma-rousseff-national-palace/|work=[[El Universal (Mexico City)|El Universal]]|date=26 May 2015|access-date=15 October 2026}}</ref> The President also attended a session of the [[Congress of the Union]]<ref>{{cite news|title=Recibirá Comisión Permanente a presidentes de Finlandia y Brasil|url=https://mexico.quadratin.com.mx/Recibira-Comision-Permanente-a-presidentes-de-Finlandia-y-Brasil|work=Quadratin México|date=20 May 2015|access-date=15 October 2026|language=es}}</ref> and visited the [[National Museum of Anthropology (Mexico)|National Museum of Anthropology]].<ref>{{cite news|title=Dilma chega ao México com agenda econômica|url=https://istoedinheiro.com.br/dilma-chega-ao-mexico-com-agenda-economica|work=[[IstoÉ Dinheiro]]|agency=[[Agence France-Presse|AFP]]|date=25 May 2015|access-date=15 October 2026|language=pt}}</ref>
|-
|{{flag|United States}}
|Washington, D.C.<br>[[Silicon Valley]]<br>New York City
|29–30 June
|{{further|Brazil–United States relations}}
President Rousseff met with President [[Barack Obama]] at the [[White House]] nearly two years after she cancelled a state visit to Washington over revelations that the United States had spied on Brazil. The two leaders sought to put the dispute behind them and to expand bilateral trade and investment, as China had overtaken the United States as Brazil's largest trading partner. Rousseff also travelled to New York to meet with investment bankers and to Silicon Valley to promote Brazil's information technology industry.<ref>[https://www.usnews.com/news/politics/articles/2015/06/29/climate-top-item-for-obama-sit-down-with-brazil-leader With dinner and monument tour, Obama, Rousseff try to show spy scandal is thing of the past] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150802184609/http://www.usnews.com/news/politics/articles/2015/06/29/climate-top-item-for-obama-sit-down-with-brazil-leader |date=2 August 2015 }} By DARLENE SUPERVILLE and ADRIANA GOMEZ LICON, Associated Press on 29 June 2015</ref><ref>[https://www.npr.org/2015/06/30/418776095/brazil-s-president-in-washington-to-patch-up-relationship-with-obama Brazil Tries To Rebuild Relations With U.S. After NSA Spying Scandal] by Jackie Northam in 30 June 2015 ([[NPR]])</ref>
|-
|{{flag|Sweden}}
|[[Stockholm]]
|18–19 October
|{{further|Brazil–Sweden relations}}
President Rousseff travelled to Sweden for an official visit. President Rousseff met with Prime Minister [[Stefan Löfven]] and King [[Carl XVI Gustaf]] of Sweden and [[Queen Silvia of Sweden]] at the [[Stockholm Palace]]. She also met with representatives from the city of [[Stockholm]] and took part in a business forum.<ref>{{cite news|title=Brazil's president visits Sweden|url=https://sverigesradio.se/artikel/6282203|access-date=19 October 2015|work=Radio Sweden|date=19 October 2015}}</ref>
|-
|{{flag|Finland}}
|[[Helsinki]]
|19–20 October
|{{further|Brazil–Finland relations}}
President Rousseff travelled to Finland for an official visit. President Rousseff met with President [[Sauli Niinistö]] at the [[Presidential Palace, Helsinki]] and also met with Prime Minister [[Juha Sipilä]].<ref>{{cite news|title=Brazilian President Rousseff Wants to Renew the Education System With Finnish Methods|url=https://finlandtoday.fi/brazilian-president-rousseff-wants-to-renew-the-education-system-with-finnish-methods/|access-date=21 October 2015|work=Finland Today|date=21 October 2015}}</ref>
|-
|{{flag|Turkey}}
|[[Antalya]]
|14–16 November
|{{further|Brazil–Turkey relations}}
President Rousseff attended the [[2015 G-20 Antalya summit|G-20 summit in Antalya]].<ref>{{cite news|last1=Pimenta|first1=Angela|title=Is Dilma Rousseff the Comeback Kid of Brazil?|url=http://observer.com/2015/11/is-president-dilma-rousseff-the-comeback-kid-of-brazil/|access-date=24 November 2015|work=[[The New York Observer]]|date=23 November 2015}}</ref>
|-
|-
|{{flag|France}}
|Paris
|30 November
|President Rousseff attended the COP21 in Paris.
|}

